          "text": "The ablations show that each design choice earns its place. Simply applying temporal reversibility to a standard MS-ResNet-34 slashes training memory from 267 down to 88 megabytes per image and cuts epoch time from 11.2 to 7.4 minutes, at the cost of only about one and a half accuracy points.",
